# Local working documents. Every markdown file except README.md stays on disk
# and out of the published repo - notes, planning, runbooks and the film
# script are working files, not product docs. The blanket rule means a new
# .md file is refused rather than silently published; re-add by exception,
# on purpose.
docs/superpowers/
*.md
!README.md
!packages/external-agent/briefs/*.md
!cases/demo/*.md
# The README's Path C points readers here for the long form: the security
# boundary, the full troubleshooting table, and what was and was not verified.
# A README citing a file the repo does not contain is a dead link on the one
# page a stranger reads first, so this one ships by exception.
!docs/EXTERNAL-AGENTS.md
